  "implementation": [
    "The native rectangular comprehension keeps the source column-then-row evaluation sequence, but stores the result at row*column_count+column. The already checked positive row count, full count product and output capacity establish a complete in-bounds bijection.",
    "Only exact successful native completion marks the private builder bank as row-major. Three-state row geometry/order shares the former two-word Option<u64> footprint. Ordinary block pushes remain column-major and retain the established permutation; a completed native bank rejects further block pushes.",
    "The original finish work, logical temporary and retained-node admission, and physical coexistence reservations remain before the direct-order branch. The unused cycle-mark allocation and swap pass are skipped. Failed/partial native attempts keep the builder unmarked and replay the original CFG.",
    "Cranelift remains the sole native emitter. The same typed banks, scalar DAG/branch emitter, prepared range factories, current immutable loans, Core constructors, checked arithmetic and bounds replay are reused. No per-cell helper, managed row/transpose materialization, source reordering, reassociation, FMA or benchmark-source rewrite is introduced.",
    "IR372 separates previously emitted column-major Objects from the new native store layout. Work141 pins the retained source permutation funding. Both exact Huffman work equations are unchanged."
  ],
